  "narrative": "The only due validation response is H103. PTEN loss is associated with stronger dependency_STAT3. The signed discovery effect R80 was +0.267 with 95% interval +0.215 to +0.319, and the independent validation R92 was +0.283 with independent interval +0.208 to +0.358. Because the claim direction -1 has been applied to the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast, a positive signed value means PTEN-loss lines have more negative dependency_STAT3 scores, i.e. stronger STAT3 dependency. The validation lower bound is far above an approximate 10% clinical-scale threshold for STAT3, so I accept and close H103. This strengthens the accepted PTEN-STAT3 association and makes the accepted subgroup-specific claims H117 and H120 more credible, but it does not validate interactions: H119 and H139 remain unresolved and closed because their interaction intervals are too wide to assess meaningful modification by PIK3CA or STK11 status. In the broader report, the robust same-dataset associations are: SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H6/H18/H19/H30/H43/H118); MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency (H8/H20/H22/H31); KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H17/H23/H24/H32/H54/H122, with QC-subset validation for H24); TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency (H49/H121, validation R52); CDKN2A loss with stronger MDM2 dependency (H59/H74/H75/H76, validations R65 and R106); and now PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency (H103/H117/H120, validation R92). These are associations within the supplied lung-lineage CRISPR dataset, not causal claims or external generalization claims. Most other registered probes are negative or inconclusive: BRAF, KRAS, EGFR, and ERBB2 alterations show near-null associations for their nominally matching or cross-pathway dependency outcomes; APC and SMAD4 probes for TMED10 and STAT3 do not support clinically meaningful stronger dependency; MTAP loss versus MDM2 is near null; RB1 loss versus DHX9 was not replicated in validation; MYC-RPL11 and MYC-WRN refinements did not confirm robust clinically meaningful effects; and many constructed research-marker interactions are null. Remaining uncertainty is concentrated in whether accepted effects are modified by co-genomic context, because main effects can be large while interaction strata are imprecise: H72 is small and wide, H119 and H139 are wide, and H116/H125 remain borderline or unconfirmed. The most informative next analysis is to spend validation budget on still-unvalidated core accepted claims, beginning with H8 MSI-high versus stronger dependency_WRN, then H6 SMARCA4 loss versus stronger dependency_SMARCA2 and H17 KEAP1 loss versus weaker dependency_NFE2L2. These validation tests are more decision-relevant than further broad mutation scans. I therefore defer H133 and register a focused MTAP interaction refinement of the CDKN2A-MDM2 axis because MTAP co-deletion is biologically adjacent to CDKN2A and may clarify whether the accepted MDM2 locus effect is CDKN2A-specific or locus co-deletion-associated.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 9 synthesize update: H103 PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 accepted and closed after validation R92. Core accepted associations: SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2; MSI-high -> stronger WRN; KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2; TP53 loss -> weaker USP7; CDKN2A loss -> stronger MDM2; PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3. Validated core claims now include TP53-USP7, CDKN2A-MDM2, and PTEN-STAT3. Still unvalidated core claims to prioritize for validation: H8 WRN MSI-high first, then H6 SMARCA2 SMARCA4 loss, then H17 or H24 for NFE2L2 KEAP1 loss. H133 deferred because validation of unvalidated core associations is more informative than further low-priority STK11-POLR2A probing. New proposal: MTAP interaction with CDKN2A effect on MDM2, parent H59, because MTAP co-deletion is the biologically adjacent refinement after the TP53 interaction H72 was small/wide. Maintain distinction between dataset associations and causality/generalizability."
